  "data": {
    "body": "Suppose that $A$ is a $3$ by $3$ real matrix having distinct real eigenvalues $\\lambda_{1}, \\lambda_{2}, \\lambda_{3}$. Which of the following statements are TRUE?\n\n\n(i) $A$ is diagonalizable.\n\n(ii) if $\\mathbf{v}_{1}, \\mathbf{v}_{2}, \\mathbf{v}_{3}$ are eigenvectors for $\\lambda_{1}, \\lambda_{2}, \\lambda_{3}$, then $\\left\\{\\mathbf{v}_{1}, \\mathbf{v}_{2}, \\mathbf{v}_{3}\\right\\}$ is an orthogonal set.\n\n(iii) if $\\mathbf{v}_{1}, \\mathbf{v}_{2}, \\mathbf{v}_{3}$ are eigenvectors for $\\lambda_{1}, \\lambda_{2}, \\lambda_{3}$, then the matrix $\\left[\\mathbf{v}_{1} \\mathbf{v}_{2} \\mathbf{v}_{3}\\right]$ is invertible. \n\n(iv) $\\operatorname{det} A=\\lambda_{1} \\lambda_{2} \\lambda_{3}$.",
    "solution": [
      4
    ],
