  "explanation": {
    "id": "8f86d338-f878-4118-a120-4e2b6f8a9b6c",
    "body": "Note: In the video, I showed a counterexample that had repeated eigenvalues, so it does not apply to the (ii) statement. The actual reasoning for this is that only real, symmetric matrices with distinct eigenvalues have orthogonal eigenvectors. There are real matrices with distinct eigenvalues that don't have orthogonal eigenvectors (play around with some numbers and you'll find this).   \n\n",
